---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import EnquiryBanner from '../components/EnquiryBanner.astro';
---
<Layout title="About Eugene Zalan — Furniture designer & maker in London" description="Meet Eugene Zalan, a furniture designer and maker based in London. Working with furniture since 2004, with an eye for sculptural form, materials and original detail." pageClass="about-page">
  <section class="about-hero shell"><div><span class="eyebrow">DESIGNER. MAKER. OBSERVER.</span><h1>A personal<br/>point of <em>view.</em></h1><p>I’m Eugene Zalan.<br/>I design and make furniture in London.</p></div><div class="about-portrait"><Photo src="/images/about/portrait.png" alt="Portrait of Eugene Zalan in London" eager sizes="(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 100vw"/></div></section>
  <section class="about-statement section shell" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">THE STARTING POINT</span><h2>The things we<br/>almost <em>walk past.</em></h2><div><p>A leaf, a small flower, the way light meets a surface. I collect these observations and translate them into form, texture and proportion.</p><p>My work is personal, but a piece also needs to belong in someone’s life. Its character must hold together with its construction and its everyday use.</p></div></section>
  <section class="about-craft shell"><div class="craft-film" data-film><video src="/videos/craft-web.mp4" poster="/media/projects/sherwood/handle-detail-1200.webp" controls muted playsinline preload="none" aria-label="Eugene Zalan detail film"></video></div><div class="about-craft-copy" data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO OBJECT</span><h2>Imagination.<br/>With an understanding<br/>of how things are made.</h2><p>I’ve worked with furniture since 2004. My experience spans design development, materials, construction and the practical decisions that turn an idea into an object.</p><p>Custom handles, legs, inlays and surface patterns give me another scale to work at — closer to jewellery, but always part of the furniture.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects">See the work <Arrow/></a></div></section>
  <section class="about-details section shell"><Photo src="/images/projects/la-clavelina/handle-isolated.png" alt="Eugene Zalan flower-shaped brass handle" sizes="(min-width: 900px) 50vw, 100vw"/><div data-reveal><span class="eyebrow">A SIGNATURE YOU CAN TOUCH</span><h2>The small things<br/>carry the idea.</h2><p>La Clavelina’s flower-shaped brass handles are designed and made by me. They connect a botanical starting point with the simple act of opening a door.</p><a class="text-link" href="/projects/la-clavelina">Explore La Clavelina <Arrow/></a></div></section>
  <EnquiryBanner title="Let’s begin a conversation."/>
</Layout>
